WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.325
The model says, “I can book Thursday.” But has anything been booked?

2
00:00:04.645 --> 00:00:07.820
In a safe voice agent, the model proposes.

3
00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:10.215
The application decides.

4
00:00:10.535 --> 00:00:12.360
Start with identity.

5
00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:17.230
The transport knows which session and participant supplied the audio.

6
00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:22.200
The model can interpret the caller’s words, but it should not invent authority.

7
00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:32.745
Before a state-changing action, the control plane verifies the customer and checks that the requested operation belongs to that customer and current call phase.

8
00:00:33.065 --> 00:00:35.840
This boundary is deliberately boring.

9
00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:39.585
Boring is good when a voice model is probabilistic.

10
00:00:39.905 --> 00:00:45.930
It turns “please book it” into a proposed operation with evidence, policy, and an owner.

11
00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:49.025
Now draw the slot and address as cards.

12
00:00:49.345 --> 00:00:52.345
The system offered Thursday from ten to noon.

13
00:00:52.665 --> 00:00:56.215
The caller confirmed that slot and the service address.

14
00:00:56.535 --> 00:01:03.785
The control plane checks that the chosen slot was actually offered and that the address came from the caller’s evidence.

15
00:01:04.105 --> 00:01:06.705
A model paraphrase is not enough.

16
00:01:07.025 --> 00:01:09.800
The same rule applies to spoken claims.

17
00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:14.045
Never say “you’re booked” before the authoritative write commits.

18
00:01:14.365 --> 00:01:17.365
A preamble may say that the system is checking.

19
00:01:17.685 --> 00:01:20.510
It must not turn an intention into a fact.

20
00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:23.705
The caller interrupts during the booking request.

21
00:01:24.025 --> 00:01:26.650
This is not only an audio problem.

22
00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:28.845
It is a write problem.

23
00:01:29.165 --> 00:01:35.090
The application needs an idempotency key so a retry does not create a duplicate job.

24
00:01:35.410 --> 00:01:41.185
It needs an explicit policy for whether an in-flight operation finishes or is cancelled.

25
00:01:41.505 --> 00:01:47.555
Then the next spoken response must describe the committed result, not the model’s previous plan.

26
00:01:47.875 --> 00:01:55.125
Observability records the trajectory: proposal, checks, backend response, retry, and final outcome.

27
00:01:55.445 --> 00:02:02.845
That trace lets evaluation ask whether the workflow was legal, not just whether the last sentence sounded confident.

28
00:02:03.165 --> 00:02:06.590
Not every request belongs in the booking workflow.

29
00:02:06.910 --> 00:02:13.060
Emergency language, a request for a human, or an unsupported case can trigger escalation.

30
00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:23.255
The control plane defines the evidence, the safety guidance allowed before transfer, the context handed to the human, and how missed escalations are measured.

31
00:02:23.575 --> 00:02:25.700
The model can detect a clue.

32
00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:28.970
The application owns the routing policy.

33
00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:37.615
That distinction keeps an OOD detector from becoming a magic classifier and keeps a safety decision out of a prompt alone.

34
00:02:37.935 --> 00:02:40.585
Finally, evaluate it repeatedly.

35
00:02:40.905 --> 00:02:46.855
Use smoke paths, capability cases, adversarial interruptions, and regression failures.

36
00:02:47.175 --> 00:02:57.250
Gate hard invariants with deterministic checks: offered slot, verified customer, grounded address, no emergency booking, and idempotent retry.

37
00:02:57.570 --> 00:03:04.495
Use human or judge review for tone and clarity, but never let a soft score override a hard invariant.

38
00:03:04.815 --> 00:03:15.290
The control plane owns identity, authorization, evidence grounding, phase state, idempotency, safety, escalation, redaction, and outcome definitions.

39
00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:17.560
The model can be swapped.

40
00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:20.855
Those responsibilities cannot disappear.

41
00:03:21.175 --> 00:03:23.425
Start with labs 02 and 07.
